{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1779070498089,"sessionID":"ses_1c7248ba4ffehv2wEvBI10NUTW","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_CNiegUKWX2pV4OmiXqj4CwDC","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Updated `CL_4023063` (`medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron`) by revising the textual definition to capture characteristic marker expression and by adding marker assertions for `LHX6` and `NKX2-1`, which are already used locally as hallmark MGE-interneuron markers.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Updated `CL_4023063` (`medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron`) in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+\n+- Revised the textual definition from a minimal developmental statement to a definition that also records characteristic marker-gene expression.\n+- Added `RO_0002292` marker assertions for:\n+  - `PR_000032148` (`LHX6`)\n+  - `PR_000032533` (`NKX2-1`)\n+\n+Rationale:\n+\n+- The imported issue explicitly requested a revised textual definition and added markers for this term.\n+- The existing term was under-modeled compared with nearby interneuron classes.\n+- Local ontology context already treats `LHX6` and `NKX2-1` as hallmark markers of MGE-derived interneurons, including in descendant and related classes such as `CL_4042013` and in supporting comments/definitions elsewhere in `cl-edit.owl`.\n+- I used local ontology evidence plus the existing cited source on the term rather than guessing new hierarchy changes.\n+\n+Validation and background work:\n+\n+- Read `__issue_context__.json` to confirm the issue scope.\n+- Inspected the existing `CL_4023063` block and neighboring MGE/CGE interneuron terms in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+- Searched the ontology for existing usage of marker assertions and for prior use of `LHX6` / `NKX2-1` with MGE-derived interneuro